                <pb facs="0806" n="794" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg794"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/2267: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-23T14:00:00-03:00">November 23, 1943—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5429. The statement issued yesterday evening (see my 5403, November 22, 4
                        p.m.)<anchor n="44" xml:id="d745-f1"/> was: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The President of the Republic convened the Cabinet this afternoon to
                            hear an exposition by the Minister of Finance concerning the recent
                            understanding with respect to Brazil’s external debt, his conclusions
                            being approved.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Souza Costa informed me last night that the Cabinet has unanimously approved all
                    of the provisions of the agreement; that President Vargas was very pleased; and
                    confirmed that the text of Decree-Law and attachments would be released to press
                    at 4:00 p.m. (Rio time), Thursday for publication Friday morning’s press.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
